# U-402 G-1 — build-context exclusions for the root runtime image.
# The Dockerfile copies the runtime tree explicitly; this file exists to keep
# the `az acr build` context small and to guarantee that excluded trees can
# never leak into the image even via a future broad COPY.

# VCS / CI / env — never send local env files to a remote builder (ACR).
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local environments (the dev .venv alone is ~757M).
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Node artifacts. `static/admin/node_modules` is ~200M after `npm ci` and the
# image rebuilds it inside a dedicated stage; `dist` is gitignored generated
# output that the spa stage produces, so sending local copies would make the
# image depend on whatever happens to be on the developer's disk. Both are
# excluded here so the Dockerfile's stage 1 is the ONLY source of those bytes.
**/node_modules
static/admin/dist

# Vendored ./pipecat — 1.1.x-era reference source tree. MUST NEVER be copied:
# `import pipecat` from /app would shadow the pip-installed pipecat-ai 1.4.0
# (same rule as deploy/deploy.sh:70 excluding it from the deploy tarball).
pipecat

# Not part of the runtime image.
tests
docs
infra
deploy
scripts
output
voice-server
node_modules

# Dev-only AWS smoke probes (smoke_bedrock/polly/transcribe/minimax.py);
# nothing in the bot import chain references them.
smoke_*.py

# Docs and misc root files the runtime never reads.
*.md
*.pdf
